---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
// Condensed patient-facing rendering of
// docs/agreements/patient-agreement-draft.md (working draft v2),
// shortened 2026-11-14. Binding terms kept; wording and non-operative
// passages cut. NEEDS-COUNSEL: confirm against the source draft before
// use. Draft-marked until the legal review gates clear (R-13).
---
<Base title="Membership agreement · Direct Lifestyle Medicine">

  <section class="page-title">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Membership agreement</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Direct Lifestyle Medicine, the practice of Logan L. DuBose, M.D.
        Texas Occupations Code chapter 162, subchapter F. Not health
        insurance.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-block:clamp(40px,5vw,64px)">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="doc-sec" style="border-top:none;padding-top:0">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>1. Our relationship</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <ul>
            <li>This creates a physician&ndash;patient relationship. Adults (18+) only. Each adult enrolls under their own agreement.</li>
            <li>This is not insurance and does not meet any insurance requirement. Keep health coverage for everything outside this agreement (section 5).</li>
            <li>I do not bill insurance, Medicare, Medicaid, or any health plan. Your coverage does not change the price or the care.</li>
            <li>You do not need another physician to enroll, and you may see other physicians at any time. With your consent, I coordinate with them.</li>
            <li>This agreement is not a promise to manage every medical condition you have.</li>
            <li><strong>Medicare and Medicaid:</strong> the arrangements for these programs are not finished, and this agreement does not state them. Before anyone on Medicare or Medicaid enrolls, I will explain in writing how it works. Nothing here claims those arrangements exist.</li>
            <li>I confirm your coverage status at enrollment and re-check it periodically.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="small soft">
            [This clause is unfinished and under review by counsel. It
            will be replaced with final terms before the agreement is
            used.]
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>2. What is included</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <ul>
            <li>Care within my scope: prevention and lifestyle medicine, acute and chronic care, prescribing, ordering and interpreting tests, mental health care within my scope, referrals, and coordination.</li>
            <li>Visits without per-visit fees or a quota. How often we meet depends on clinical need and my judgment.</li>
            <li>Portal messages, answered within 1&ndash;2 business days. Urgent needs follow section 4.</li>
            <li>Home visits within my service area [published at launch], when I judge an exam requires it. Clinic visits for exams and procedures that need equipment.</li>
            <li>An annual review.</li>
            <li>Forms and paperwork, including disability, FMLA, insurance forms, letters, and prior authorizations.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>3. What I do not promise</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <ul>
            <li>24/7, evening, or weekend availability.</li>
            <li>Emergency or urgent response (section 4).</li>
            <li>Specific outcomes.</li>
            <li>Hospital care. Hospital physicians manage admissions. I stay informed and coordinate afterward.</li>
            <li>That every request fits the membership (section 6).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>4. Emergencies, urgent needs, and time away</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Emergency:</strong> call 911 or go to the ER for chest pain, stroke symptoms, severe breathing trouble, major injury, uncontrolled bleeding, thoughts of self-harm, or anything life-threatening. Never wait for me.</li>
            <li><strong>Urgent:</strong> use urgent care or another physician. Tell me afterward.</li>
            <li><strong>Routine:</strong> message me.</li>
            <li><strong>Time away:</strong> up to about three months a year, with advance notice. While away, I check results and messages periodically and arrange refills before I go.</li>
            <li>If I suddenly cannot practice, you will be notified promptly, your records stay available, and billing pauses.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>5. What the fee does not cover</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <p>Billed by others, usually through your insurance:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>labs (discounted cash prices passed through at my cost, disclosed first)</li>
            <li>imaging and other tests</li>
            <li>medicines and vaccines (Texas law does not let me dispense)</li>
            <li>specialists, therapists, and other clinicians</li>
            <li>urgent care, ER, hospital, and ambulance</li>
            <li>medical equipment and supplies</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Whether HSA or FSA funds can pay the fee is not settled.
            Confirm with your tax advisor.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>6. Other charges</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <p>I tell you before anything is charged.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Home visits outside my service area are not offered. We use video or a clinic visit.</li>
            <li>Procedure supplies are passed through at my cost, stated first.</li>
            <li>No no-show or late-cancellation fees.</li>
            <li>If you need near-daily physician contact for an extended period, we discuss whether this practice is still the right level of care. There is no added fee.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>7. Scope</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <ul>
            <li>I co-manage conditions that need ongoing specialist care. I refer for psychiatric care, substance-use treatment beyond primary care, and anything needing rapid in-person response or continuous monitoring. If your needs outgrow this practice, I help you move to the right care (section 9).</li>
            <li>Controlled substances are prescribed only under a written policy, including in-person, monitoring, and agreement requirements.</li>
            <li>I must be licensed where you are during a visit. My license covers Texas [finalized at launch]. Tell me if you travel or move. Moving may end eligibility.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>8. Payment</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <ul>
            <li>$99 per month, per adult, charged in advance each month to a card or bank account on file. A payment method on file is required. Annual prepay is available at the same price.</li>
            <li>A reduced fee or no fee is available where $99 is a barrier. It is agreed before you enroll and written into your copy of this agreement. The care and all other terms are the same at every fee.</li>
            <li>No enrollment fee. No minimum commitment.</li>
            <li>If a payment fails, you get notice and [a set number of] days to update it before membership pauses.</li>
            <li>You may re-enroll after cancelling, without a fee, if the panel has room.</li>
            <li>Fee changes require 60 days&rsquo; written notice and take effect at a future renewal.</li>
            <li>This agreement and the published price are your Good Faith Estimate as a self-pay patient under federal law.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>9. Ending the membership</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>You</strong> may cancel anytime through the portal or in writing, effective at the end of the paid month.</li>
            <li><strong>I</strong> may end the membership with 30 days&rsquo; written notice. I stay available for urgent and active issues during that time.</li>
            <li>Either way, active workups are completed or handed off with a written summary, prescriptions are bridged up to 90 days where safe, and your records are sent promptly to you and your next physician. An electronic copy is always free.</li>
            <li>Charges stop when membership ends. Annual prepay: unused full months are refunded.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="doc-sec">
        <div class="sh">
          <h2>10. Other terms</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="sc">
          <p>
            Privacy notice (HIPAA) and telemedicine consent are provided
            separately. Portal terms apply. Texas law governs. This is
            the entire agreement. The fee may not be assigned to
            insurance.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Signatures</strong>: patient &middot; physician
            &middot; date &middot; payment authorization.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="inner">
        <a class="btn btn-inverse" href="/book">Book a free conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
